<<~ aka uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/lararium-canonical-model`>>



<<~ ahu slot=`#/entry`>>

! mempalace ~ the guest comparator and the library shore

''The lararium owns its memory Sensorium.'' Its append-only content records shall hold the AI–operator journey; its structure, form, persistence and worldline capabilities shall read that journey at their own grains. Bounded Claude and Liliʻuokalani book trials now carry frozen custody, typed occurrences, owned MiniLM Content and separate full-constituency li bases in disposable roots. The meaning braid, KI, live collection and founded persistent root remain open. The pinned mempalace Python package supplies storage, embedding and search functions to the local holders. The upstream installation at `~/.mempalace/palace` stands separately as a ''guest comparator'', raised by an operator act and never written by the Sensorium's capture path.

''Alpha destination — the two-reader strangler fig.'' The Memory Sensorium gradually takes the Lararium memory read route as each source slice earns custody, coverage, retrieval and recovery witnesses. The upstream guest remains a required independent comparator in this operator's alpha development, while its installation and store remain optional for later end users. Both readers shall consume every discoverable existing AI–operator conversation and new conversations on each supported host and harness. A bounded fixture tests a slice; it never narrows the destination. Missing or inaccessible history receives a named gap or unknown at a declared horizon, not a silent completeness claim. The guest mines vanilla from the same inventoried source evidence and keeps its own projection, config and lifecycle; the owned Sensorium keeps typed occurrences, source-backed relations and derived readings. Neither reader repairs the other's missed source by borrowing its answer.

''The upstream base.'' The pinned submodule names upstream `develop` at `d9bf01e` on local branch `dev/sdm-upstream-base`. The `dev/sdm-integration` merge at `1798186` stands outside the runtime dependency: its extra daemon, NDJSON adapter, lazy embedder, search-hit metadata and test changes carry no implicit authority into this branch. A capability returns only after a fresh contract and a witness against the pinned upstream API. The upstream hook scripts carry no pause check (their patch rests preserved); the Lararium's own hook pause path stays a separate concern.

Three memory registers continue to pull against one another: the verbatim journey in the owned Sensorium, curated `CLAUDE.md` / `MEMORY.md` / `AGENTS.md` conclusions, and the lararium quine's domain canon. Recall may compare them and surface conflict; no register silently overwrites another. The fuller relation stands at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/lararium-memory`>>.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/boundary`>>

!! One library, two stores, separate authority

The vendored Python package rides behind a local causal-island boundary. The Node coordinator names a Sensorium root, spawns holders and reads receipts; the Python machina consumes the library and owns content/structure/form computation. A holder's process does not make the upstream guest its store: every sovereign read and write names the owned root beneath `<lararium>/sensoriums/<name>`. The memory instance resolves under `<lararium>/sensoriums/memory`; each corpus or other input stream composes its own store. Sensoriums do not federate. Only a deliberate operator Act may carry a distilled finding out to a federated surface.

The guest comparator remains a separately tended upstream palace at `~/.mempalace/palace` on a host. `lares mempalace setup` raises it deliberately and pins `hooks.auto_save=false`; `lares mempalace harvest` fills it with vanilla transcript drawers for comparison. Upstream 3.10 moved fresh installs to XDG config and palace homes while preserving detected legacy installs: the guest door must explicitly name its config and palace roots before a fresh post-merge setup can claim this legacy path. In the container, `HOME=/state` changes what `~` names, so an alpha guest needs an explicitly mounted guest root and config; a host spelling cannot serve as an implicit container path. `lares sense` addresses the sovereign Sensorium. The comparator never supplies the owned store's ground truth, and a re-pour of either store never reaches the other by an ambient default.

''The good tensegrity cut survives at the right address:'' verbatim drawers keep what happened; derived bearings, annotations and projections make them traversable. The `lar_*` enrichment schema belongs to the sovereign Sensorium's telemetry and capture flow, not to a blanket writeback into the guest. An enrichment version changes with its transform; a replay keeps stable source identity so it does not mint duplicate drawers under a renamed stage path.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/capability-settlement`>>

!! Re-earn capabilities against the upstream pin

The old fork's commits are an evidence shelf, not a patch queue. The upstream pin already carries the config-directory override and the RFC-002 source registry; the Lararium may consume those documented entry points after an adapter witness. The fork's NDJSON source adapter and `mine --source` daemon forwarding do not define the sovereign capture route. The Sensorium's own source caps read native harness records and land into its owned root; an upstream source adapter is useful only if a future guest-comparator operation actually needs it. The old lazy-embedder flag has no handler in the pin and is no longer exported by the holder cap. Search-hit metadata and daemon contention behavior need separate API and load probes before a parent feature depends on them.

The redesign crosses these gates in order:

# ''Source identity.'' A host adapter names surface, harness, native session/thread, execution host, format version and source event; it sends a stable pointer or staged bytes across the container boundary.
# ''Durable ground.'' The intake cursor advances only after raw evidence and its receipt commit; the typed-content frontier advances after the trial ledger lands parsed blocks; the semantic-view frontier advances after the owned Content holder verifies its rows. Retry replays the same intent at each boundary. The guest comparator never joins this write path.
# ''Causal reading.'' Given turn, subagent, fork, handback and related-session events become typed edges with provenance; unknown edges remain unknown. Annotation and retrieval derive from the landed ground.
# ''Capability proof.'' Test each pinned MemPalace API the holder calls, then probe live Claude, Codex and Copilot payloads on every claimed host surface. A feature that passes a unit fixture but has no accessible producer remains unclaimed.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/capture`>>

!! Capture reads native sources, then lands once per source identity

The current memory source caps read Claude and Codex JSONL, Copilot CLI SQLite, and Copilot VS Code event streams. This list describes existing adapters, not complete coverage. Current Copilot CLI documentation places a fuller event log under `~/.copilot/session-state/<session-id>/events.jsonl` and describes `session-store.db` as cross-session data; Codex documents its hook transcript pointer but warns that the transcript format may change. Each harness source therefore needs its own versioned adapter and a probe before it claims completeness. Live capture and bulk replay must enter one custody and projection contract: source evidence → typed verbatim blocks → model-backed Content view → versioned readings. The source-intake cursor advances after raw evidence and its receipt commit; the typed-content frontier advances after the SQLite ledger transaction; the semantic-view frontier advances only after the owned Content view lands and verifies its blocks. None claims that another has caught up. The frozen Claude pair and complete Liliʻuokalani book have each reached a verified owned semantic view in disposable trials; live collection and reconciled source coverage remain open.

A chat-harness source envelope retains the declared surface and harness, native session ID, thread/agent ID where supplied, event or format version, execution host, source pointer and source event identity. A book source instead names its work, edition, digital witness, portable library locator and exact byte revision; it does not invent a native chat session ID. `cwd` contributes routing context; it does not stand alone as session identity. The harness's turn and subagent events supply the Beat and causal edges when present. A missing edge stays unknown, never inferred from prose. A related chat, fork, or remote session names a new graph relation, never a duplicate drawer. These are redesign contracts; today's parsers have not yet earned all of them. See the current [Claude hook reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks), [Codex hook reference](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks), and [Copilot CLI directory reference](https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/reference/copilot-cli-reference/cli-config-dir-reference).

Static corpus Sensoriums use the same composition with a different source and order declaration. The memory rhizome receives its turn Beat and fork/handback edges from the harness; a corpus with no grounded Beat must earn any temporal reading. The design of record, including li/ki limits, stands at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/sensorium-machina`>>.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/hooks`>>

!! Pause the minting, drain the holders

`lares hooks pause` writes `<state>/hooks.paused`; the parent ingest hook checks that marker before starting a job. The upstream hook scripts now match upstream `develop` and carry no Lararium pause check. The marker stops new Lararium hook work, but never proves an existing holder drained or an independently enabled upstream hook stopped. A teardown or comparator re-pave must pause its actual intake, drain and verify holders, act on the named store, then resume only the intake it held. Host hooks and a containerized vessel inhabit different path namespaces; a host marker does not automatically appear under `/state`.

The current `lares mempalace repave` still expects the operator to quiesce holders first. Its preview's quiesce wording must not be read as an enacted drain. The current operator lifecycle and measure-first law stand at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/sensorium-runbook`>>.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/container-crossing`>>

!! The container crossing carries a Python seat and still needs source ingress

The surface vessel mounts `/state` for durable house data and `/workspace` for the corpus. The `serve` image now carries Node output, an installed Python 3.12 seat, the pinned MemPalace package and Sensorium scripts; an image witness exercised a holder and MCP v2 against disposable state. Model bytes need explicit verified provisioning, and R engines remain unclaimed. Host transcript paths still need a bounded host collector and a read-only handoff before a container can consume them: current shared discovery resolves under the process home, which points at `/state` inside this image rather than at host Claude, Codex or Copilot history. The memory store stays under `/state/data/lararium/sensoriums/memory`; the alpha guest comparator takes a separate explicit mount and lifecycle.

The deployment keeps Node-supervised stdio holders. The host collector must copy or stream only an explicitly named source into an intake under `/state`; the vessel verifies its declared source identity and reads that intake without assuming the host's home path exists inside the container. The source adapter owns parsing; the Sensorium owns derived records; the guest comparator owns neither. A later independent Python service would earn a new versioned transport, health and store-ownership contract. The packaged seat proves a runtime crossing, not live source coverage or an operational memory Sensorium.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/redesign-plan`>>

!! The redesign plan ~ source evidence, owned ground, earned readings

''Status: PLAN, not a claim of deployed coverage.'' This plan starts from the clean upstream pin and the present Sensorium code. It preserves the memory and li/ki intent while replacing assumptions tied to one WSL home, one mutable transcript path, and our retired MemPalace fork. One operator holds the alpha; the old derived palaces have been burned. The first trials build fresh disposable Sensoriums over bounded inputs; the authorized destination covers all discoverable old and new conversations, progressively by producer and host, and the persistent memory root waits for the parallel Lararium's founding and repeated proofs. Native AI chat history remains untouched throughout. Each phase has an observable exit; a green fixture without a reachable producer leaves that surface unclaimed. The host may receive hook signals; the container holds `/state` and `/workspace`; the guest comparator remains an operator-raised separate store, required for this alpha. The current execution order sits at #/provisional-roadmap.

''Golden rules.'' Producer bytes precede interpretation. An occurrence names ''which act'', a digest names ''which bytes'', and an observation names ''when this version was seen''. A block ID binds source identity, byte revision, parser version and block position; its text digest travels separately. An intake cursor proves custody of raw evidence; a typed-content frontier proves landing in the trial ledger; a semantic-view frontier proves landing in the owned model-backed Content view. None stands in for another. Retries reuse intent IDs and return prior receipts. Inventory bounds every completeness claim by source and horizon. Every derived reading carries its algorithm/model/basis version and a path to its evidence. Locality follows the actual execution host and store mount. The shortcuts that fail these rules include path-as-identity, hash-as-occurrence, digest-as-causal-edge, hook-success-as-complete-capture, cursor-before-commit, silent parser skip, mutable-transcript-as-permanent-WAL, and an end-to-end `exactly once` promise across unrelated stores.

!!! ① Name the source before giving it a parser

Build a capability inventory for each ''harness × surface × execution host × installed version'': discoverability, native session/thread/agent IDs, source format, hook events, retention settings, compaction behavior, local or remote execution, permissions, and how a full inventory can be replayed. Start with local Claude Code, local Codex, Copilot CLI, and VS Code Copilot; cloud and remote targets receive `unknown` or `unsupported` until a supported source and a live probe exist. A hook wakes capture but never certifies that a local transcript exists or that its bytes remain available. A periodic inventory reconciles the hook's hints with native sources.

The October research changes three starting assumptions. Claude supplies `transcript_path` and `agent_transcript_path` in documented hooks, while [an environment setting](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/env-vars) can suppress local prompt history. Codex's `transcript_path` may be null and its format is explicitly unstable. Copilot CLI documents per-session `events.jsonl` plus a separately managed SQLite cross-session index; VS Code and SDK-backed harnesses need their own adapter claims. A path found on one host never certifies another host's coverage. See #/grounds.

!!! ② Give occurrence, evidence, and observation different names

One ''source namespace'' names the actual producer instance and execution host, never a staging path. Within it, a ''logical locator'' names an occurrence: use the producer's stable message/event ID where one is documented and probed; otherwise declare a source generation plus record position/byte range or row key. A content hash does not identify an occurrence: two separate turns can carry equal bytes.

An ''evidence revision'' names `(source namespace, logical locator, raw-byte hash)`. It keeps the exact source bytes and parser-independent provenance: source generation or snapshot hash, original path or API resource as a sighting, byte range or SQLite row key where meaningful, and collection method/version. An ''observation'' records that an adapter saw this revision at a particular inventory pass. Its stable retry intent returns the earlier receipt; the same intent with different bytes is a conflict, requiring a new observation intent and an explicit revision. A later A→B→A at one locator makes three observations over two byte revisions, with the supersession chain on the observations. A changed hash under one logical locator is a revision to preserve, never an overwrite of an append-only drawer or a silent `is_landed` skip.

The current `sha256(source_file)_chunk` cid is a source-position key. Its `lar_chain` detects changed bytes, but muting that cid alone cannot give the new bytes an appendable identity. The redesign must key new content on evidence revision identity and keep the currently selected observation separate from historical verbatim evidence. The old derived palaces were burned, so the alpha pilot has no legacy-cid migration; a future retained store would need its own explicit migration witness. A path rename and an intake copy must not mint a new occurrence. If a producer offers no stable native ID, the adapter's fallback locator and its limitations become part of the receipt.

!!! ③ Cross the host/container shore with a durable intake

Prefer a small host collector with read access only to declared harness sources. It stages exact source evidence into an authenticated local intake under the host directory mounted as `/state`; no host transcript path is handed to a container as though both namespaces shared one home. It reports an explicit ephemeral verdict ''per session'' before staging lasting content, including a SQLite-backed Copilot session; a `.jsonl` filename suffix cannot decide that policy. Scratch work kept blind by its launcher never enters the memory intake. Logs and receipts carry identifiers and counts, not transcript text.

The intake keeps a source snapshot or generation manifest and exact record bytes with offsets where the native format permits. Retain a full generation snapshot where parsing depends on cross-record context or a format remains uncertain; use bounded record slices only after an adapter witness shows they permit faithful reparse. JSONL takes complete line bytes and records any torn tail as uncommitted. A live SQLite database is read through a consistent SQLite backup or read transaction, not a raw `cp` of its main file while a WAL may hold committed rows. A future API source keeps its response bytes and API cursor with the same scoped receipt law. The byte unit, retention footprint and source-specific recovery route are measured in phase ①; an oversized or unavailable source yields an explicit coverage limit, never silent truncation. The host collector owns a restricted intake directory; the container accepts only descriptors naming an allowed adapter and paths beneath that root, with source lengths and hashes checked before a receipt. Source-specific readers get only the source access they require, and the host collector receives no general palace-write authority.

For modest evidence, put raw bytes, uniqueness receipt, source snapshot/coverage, intake cursor and a durable projection intent in ONE local SQLite transaction under `/state`. The intake cursor may advance once ''that'' transaction commits, even if the asynchronous content projector later fails; the projector then reports lag and retries. If a measured source requires external blob files, use a recoverable same-filesystem protocol: write a unique temporary file, verify length/hash, `fsync` it, publish without replacing an existing hash path, `fsync` the parent directory, then commit its reference and receipt in SQLite. Recovery removes only unreferenced old blobs after a grace period and flags any referenced missing or mismatched blob. A plain rename can overwrite its target, and an atomic rename alone does not promise durable bytes.

One local writer serializes the intake transaction. The state mount must sit on a local Linux filesystem; a WSL distro's Linux filesystem and a `/mnt/c` mount do not offer the same filesystem semantics. Use WAL with `synchronous=FULL` if choosing WAL; do not infer power-loss survival from a kill-9 test. The host-to-container transport remains at-least-once. The receipt binds intent ID, source namespace, locator, source generation, byte hash and length, observation ID and committed intake cursor. An exact intent retry returns that receipt; an intent with different evidence fails closed and is surfaced for adapter reconciliation. A new observation intent records changed bytes under the same occurrence. No end-to-end exactly-once claim crosses the host, intake SQLite, content store and any outside effect.

!!! ④ Project once per evidence revision and algorithm version

The intake archive holds producer evidence; the typed ledger preserves parsed verbatim text and flat metadata; the owned Content view carries model-backed search over those blocks. The trial projector already lands blocks under `(source key, evidence revision, parser version, block ordinal)` with a stable key and a contiguous typed-content frontier. The bounded Claude and book projectors also land independently receipted owned MiniLM Content views; their semantic frontiers name those views without claiming live coverage. A parse failure gets a durable, visible quarantine disposition with its evidence pointer and parser version; it cannot advance a successful frontier as a silent skip. A separate semantic-view receipt and frontier must follow verified Content landing. Structure, form, worldline, embeddings, lexical views and annotations derive from that ground under their own named algorithm/model/basis versions; their failure leaves a retryable intent and an honest lag reading. A reparse reads the original source bytes, creates a new projection version and keeps old results inspectable until a deliberate switch. Replay sends no external effect by accident; a deliberate outward act needs its own durable outbox identity and operator authority.

A worldline edge carries its type, source evidence pointers, source IDs and provenance grade: `source-declared`, `hook-observed`, or `inferred`. Subagent spawn, handback, fork, injection and related-session links can have multiple predecessors or an unresolved parent. Timestamp order, file adjacency and an FFZ address alone never assert a causal edge. The harness-given Beat stays distinct from a derived rhythmic boundary. A reader may inspect the historical observation and revision even when current recall favors the latest one.

!!! ⑤ Report the area actually observed

Per source instance, retain inventory generation, native cursor if offered, observed snapshot/hash, scanned range or row set, intake receipt frontier, content projection frontier, last reconciliation and any missing interval. Coverage reads `observed`, `reconciled`, `gap`, or `unknown` over a named source and horizon. `Reconciled` means a stable inventory at that horizon matched committed evidence; it never means every session the vendor ever held. Rotation, truncation, retention expiry, disabled history, a lost remote host or an expired API cursor may force a fresh inventory and may leave a permanent gap. Report that gap rather than filling it from adjacent timestamps or calling an empty scan complete.

The pause lever stops new Lararium intake work. Draining must separately witness in-flight host collectors, intake transactions and content projectors before a re-pour or teardown. Resume only what the operation paused. The runbook's measure-first law still governs before/after comparisons: a later replay can restore retained bytes but cannot recreate a baseline never taken.

!!! ⑥ Earn the library and the image seat

Keep upstream MemPalace pinned as a dependency, probe the exact imports and methods each holder calls, and version those probes with the pin. The product image now packages the Python interpreter, pinned dependencies, MemPalace package and Sensorium scripts; repeat holder and stdio witnesses against each promoted image with `/state` and `/workspace` mounted. The Node coordinator names roots, supervises and reads receipts; the Python holder owns source parsing and store computation. A second Python service remains a later transport decision, not a prerequisite for this redesign.

The guest comparator keeps its own config, palace, hooks and lifecycle. It can consume a deliberate export for a comparison, but its result never supplies a missing source event, overwrites the owned ground, or silently becomes a Sensorium dependency. The old fork's NDJSON and lazy-embedder changes return only if a measured need and an upstream-compatible API justify them.

!!! Ordered implementation and exit witnesses

These are technical exit witnesses; #/provisional-roadmap gives the alpha execution order and its promotion gates.

# ''Inventory.'' Record the installed versions, settings, source roots, IDs, format samples, retention, ephemeral evidence and access rights for the four local surfaces. Exit when each adapter row names `documented`, `probed`, `inferred`, or `unknown` per capability; cloud rows remain honest unknowns.
# ''Identity and custody.'' Define the source namespace, logical locator, byte revision, observation, intake receipt and current-revision view. Exercise A→B→A and staging-path renames on a fresh trial store. Exit when immutable evidence and retry identity survive both.
# ''Container and intake.'' Keep the packaged Python seat; stand a restricted host collector and `/state` receipt store for live sources. Exit when the mounted product container accepts a replayed source, answers one receipt, recovers each crash cut and leaves the submodule tree clean.
# ''Adapters and reconciliation.'' Migrate Claude and Codex local JSONL, Copilot CLI session files/SQLite and VS Code by harness version. Hooks trigger; inventory verifies. Exit per surface only after live hook and bulk inventory produce the same evidence identities and explicit gaps.
# ''Content and causal projection.'' Re-land typed blocks from evidence revisions, project independently versioned planes, and attach only evidence-backed worldline edges. Exit when reparse and projector failure preserve old bytes and report lag without duplicate outward work.
# ''Operations and comparator.'' Wire pause/drain/verify/resume, coverage status and the before/after baseline. Raise the guest only through its deliberate command. Exit when a re-pour proves source count, evidence count, content count and claimed coverage agree at a named horizon.

!!! Six required adversarial witnesses

# ''Rewrite and return.'' At one source locator ingest A, then B, then A again: three observations, two immutable byte revisions, an A→B→A observation chain, current A, historical B; re-sending any intent adds no duplicate. The new content key admits B without overwriting A.
# ''Crash at every intake cut.'' Stop after partial temp, verified temp, publication, directory sync, precommit and postcommit/preack. No receipt points to missing bytes; retry returns one receipt; orphan cleanup never removes a referenced blob. If the first implementation uses SQLite BLOBs only, test its transaction cuts and add blob-file cuts when that route is enabled.
# ''Live source and ephemeral.'' Snapshot a Copilot SQLite database during a concurrent write through its backup API; parse a consistent snapshot and classify a SQLite-only scratch session from its session metadata. A torn JSONL final line remains pending rather than counted as evidence.
# ''Loss and reconciliation.'' Truncate, rotate and edit a JSONL; suppress local history and expire a simulated API cursor. Inventory discovers revisions or marks a bounded gap, never advances `reconciled` past an unknown interval, and never treats absence of a file as proof the session never existed.
# ''Projection failure and replay.'' Inject failure after raw intake commit and during a v2 parser/projector run. Intake cursor may advance; projection frontier stays behind and reports lag. Original bytes and v1 results survive; retry completes v2 once with no outbound effect.
# ''Causal disagreement.'' Main session → subagent → handback with a missing parent, conflicting IDs and skewed timestamps. Only source-backed edges assert reachability; inferred links stay labeled and removable; changing FFZ placement cannot change the source-declared DAG.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/provisional-roadmap`>>

!! Strangler-fig alpha roadmap ~ one read route at a time

''Standing.'' This is the execution order for the one-operator alpha, not a declaration that the final Lararium or its persistent memory palace already stands. The old derived palaces have been burned; no compatibility migration earns a place in the first trial. The parallel Lararium crew owns founding, keys, vessel startup and its broader image lifecycle. This Sensorium work owns source ingress, dependency closure, the Python/R seat, stores, projections and their receipts. The crews exchange an image digest, code-root/interpreter contract, `/state` ownership and one joint mounted-runtime witness before a persistent handoff. The guest MemPalace comparator stays a separate, deliberate operation.

''Never-burn boundary.'' Native Claude JSONL, Codex, Copilot and other AI chat history stay read-only and outside every Sensorium teardown target. The operator's separate per-machine history-stamping repository remains independent of this work. A trial may discard its copied intake evidence and derived store ''after'' the named test series and its receipts finish; until then, its frozen evidence manifest and exact selected bytes must survive every rebuild, crash probe and comparison. A trial never deletes or edits the native source. The founded memory Sensorium gets its own durable evidence, state and backup contract rather than inheriting a trial directory by renaming it.

''Four-pass code reading, 2026-10-18.'' Yin first traced host discovery, hooks, guest mining and container mounts; Yang first traced the sovereign legacy holder and the frozen custody, typed and Content trials. They then exchanged seams and challenged one another's findings. The shared `session_discovery.py` yields paths, not a common immutable source snapshot: empty or failed roots can look like no sources, and the guest can report `ok` despite dropped files. The guest explicitly lacks the sovereign's JSONL ephemeral gate, while that gate itself cannot classify a Copilot SQLite-only scratch session. The trial owned Content writes the same rooted Chroma store that live recall can open, so there is no necessary store-format wall; orchestration, frontier-aware reads and metadata/filter compatibility remain unproved. These corrections order the backlog below.

''Done evidence, not a deployment claim.'' The frozen Claude parent and child have 1,717 matching typed, owned MiniLM Content and full-constituency li occurrences in disposable roots; the complete Liliʻuokalani witness has 40 typed spans and 38 selected literary Content/li occurrences. A source revision and observation ledger, independent semantic receipts and model asset checks stand for those trials. Legacy `sense` recall, hooks, sweep, worldline and kapae remain useful but still travel the old CID/store route. The product image has the Python seat, yet `HOME=/state` makes its `~/.claude`, `~/.codex` and `~/.copilot` discovery roots container-local. No live collector or full-history reconciliation has been witnessed.

!!! Kanban policy and four delivery waves

Pull a source slice only with a named host, harness, surface, producer version, source horizon, expected reader set and disposable or founded store root. Keep its card in ''inventory → custody → typed → semantic → serving → reconciled''; a failed or unknown stage stays visible with its receipt and never inherits the next stage's status. Each wave ends in a mounted-runtime demonstration, a count/identity reconciliation for ''both'' independent readers, and a published gap list. A hook is a wake-up hint; inventory sets the completeness boundary. Do not promote a later wave from a green bounded fixture alone.

''Wave 1 · Make one frozen occurrence serve.'' Bring the existing frozen Claude intake→typed→owned MiniLM Content path under one Node-supervised product operation in a disposable mounted `/state` memory root. Query the known occurrence through the actual `lares sense` or MCP recall door, checking CID, text, source/revision metadata, filters and honest unsupported views. Exact retry adds nothing; A→B→A preserves two byte revisions and three observations; projector failure reports lag; a cold image restart still answers the query. The guest is independently fed vanilla from that same named evidence generation and reports its own mine receipt. This slice proves the read-route seam before more li, ki or source adapters are required for promotion.

''Wave 1 working evidence and open gate.'' A named disposable trial operation now supervises frozen Claude custody, typed projection and owned MiniLM Content, then serves `lares sense search/status --trial-root` through the real CLI. The complete parent fixture landed 1,697 receipted Content CIDs from 9,848,331 frozen source bytes; a fresh CLI process retrieved text, CID, source and revision at typed and semantic frontiers 1/1. Trial search rechecks exact current observation membership against the custody ledger and marks bounded candidate filtering non-exhaustive. A separate vanilla guest mined 1,000 drawers from the same source digest and found a distinctive passage, but its mine stdout receipt was lost; the two readers therefore have no complete count/identity reconciliation yet. Focused crash, lock, membership and holder-shutdown tests pass. A mounted product-image restart is still unproved: the Docker build was refused by buildx home-directory write access before the Dockerfile ran. Keep this card at ''serving trial'', with the mounted-runtime and guest-receipt gates open; do not infer live ingress or a founded store.

''Next sprint · Close Wave 1 before pulling live history.'' First obtain an authorized writable buildx state and build the pinned product image; run the same frozen operation with a mounted disposable `/state`, then restart the image and query the receipted occurrence cold. Preserve image digest, code root, interpreter, model asset identity, mount ownership and operation receipts. In parallel, rerun the independent vanilla guest against the exact frozen evidence generation with an explicit guest config and root, save its mine receipt, and publish a two-reader source/identity table with explained cardinality differences. Verify A→B→A, exact retry, projection failure and recovery in the mounted runtime. Mark Wave 1 reconciled only when those witnesses and its gap list are attached; then pull Wave 2's single live Claude host slice.

''Wave 2 · Bring one live host across, twice.'' Stand a restricted host collector and authenticated `/state` intake for one Claude producer/version/host. Snapshot exact source bytes once per generation; feed the sovereign and guest from that receipt while keeping the guest's palace/config separately mounted and vanilla. Make both readers use one per-session ephemeral verdict before staging. A live completed conversation and a bounded backfill batch traverse the same route; hook hints reconcile with inventory. Report root absence, access or parse failure as `unknown`/`gap`, never empty success; any dropped guest source fails a complete verdict. Show one restart, crash cut, pause/drain and matched two-reader source horizon without touching native history.

''Wave 3 · Expand coverage and backfill.'' Add Codex, Copilot CLI per-session `events.jsonl` and consistent SQLite snapshot reading, then VS Code Copilot by witnessed host/version adapters. Inventory all discoverable old conversations on each supported host and reconcile new live ones at declared horizons. Classify SQLite-only scratch sessions, preserve torn-tail and source-loss gaps, and publish source/evidence/typed/semantic/guest counts per reader. Replay full history in bounded receipted batches into a ''fresh'' durable memory root after the parallel Lararium founding witness; never rename the disposable trial. Every adapter reaches an actual mounted runtime and cold-restart proof before its surface is called covered. Remote/cloud rows remain explicit unknowns until an accessible source is evidenced.

''Wave 4 · Earn the richer memory and promotion.'' Move source-backed fork, subagent, handback, injection and related-session edges onto occurrence evidence; preserve old recall and reversible kapae through new interfaces. Build the meaning braid with separate DECLARED, ENACTED and USED warrants; retain the witnessed full-constituency li basis, then earn ki under its own boundary, null and support controls. Keep FFZ placement separate from causal order. Probe retrieval quality, resource slope, basis drift, reparse, crash recovery, backup/restore and repeated image builds. The parallel Lararium crew provides founding, key and vessel witnesses; this crew provides source ingress, state, model and reader witnesses. Exchange image digest, code root, interpreter, `/state` ownership and one joint end-to-end receipt before the owned route becomes primary. The guest remains required for alpha comparison and optional for later users.

''Promotion rule.'' Set numeric bounds for coverage gaps, projection lag, retrieval, recovery and resource use before reading the results. Publish passes, failures and unknowns for both readers at the same horizon without borrowing one reader's missing source from the other. Books prove corpus machinery; a selected chat week proves only its selected horizon. A batch's `--all` never certifies all history. Route memory reads through the owned Sensorium only after its serving, full-history reconciliation and restore witnesses pass; keep the older route available for comparison until that cutover is observed.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/grounds`>>

!! Prior-art grounds and the limits of their rhyme

CloudEvents [source plus id](https://github.com/cloudevents/spec/blob/v1.0.2/cloudevents/spec.md) and GitHub's [redelivery ID practice](https://docs.github.com/en/webhooks/using-webhooks/best-practices-for-using-webhooks) inform stable retry intent; neither guarantees a harness supplies a usable native message ID. [Debezium's snapshot-to-stream handoff](https://debezium.io/documentation/reference/stable/connectors/postgresql.html) and [Kubernetes watch recovery](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/using-api/api-concepts) inform inventory plus cursor reconciliation; Claude, Codex and Copilot do not thereby become CDC databases. [SQLite's commit](https://www.sqlite.org/atomiccommit.html), [WAL](https://www.sqlite.org/wal.html), [synchronous modes](https://www.sqlite.org/pragma.html#pragma_synchronous), [backup API](https://www.sqlite.org/backup.html), Linux [file and directory sync](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/fsync.2.html) and [no-replace rename](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/rename.2.html) bound the proposed local durability protocol; the actual WSL and host mount still need a fault probe. [Event Sourcing](https://martinfowler.com/eaaDev/EventSourcing.html) informs replayable projections, while the [outbox pattern](https://debezium.io/documentation/reference/stable/transformations/outbox-event-router.html) keeps outside effects separate. [W3C PROV-DM](https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-dm/) and [OpenTelemetry trace links](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/otel/trace/api/) inform typed, evidence-backed worldline relations. The official [Claude](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks), [Codex](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks) and [Copilot CLI](https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/reference/copilot-cli-reference/cli-config-dir-reference) references bound the initial surface claims. Every mapping here is a Lararium design inference until its producer and crash witnesses pass.

